"use strict";(self.webpackChunkphyling_docs=self.webpackChunkphyling_docs||[]).push([[4630],{3710:(e,t,a)=>{a.r(t),a.d(t,{comp:()=>o,data:()=>r});var i=a(641);const n={},o=(0,a(6262).A)(n,[["render",function(e,t){return(0,i.uX)(),(0,i.CE)("div",null,[...t[0]||(t[0]=[(0,i.Fv)('<h1 id="maxi-phyling" tabindex="-1"><a class="header-anchor" href="#maxi-phyling"><span>Maxi-Phyling</span></a></h1><h2 id="overview" tabindex="-1"><a class="header-anchor" href="#overview"><span>Overview</span></a></h2><p>This is the heart of Phyling technology: a unique, versatile unit that records all your data at high frequency. Compact, it fits anywhere. Its processing power allows it to send and analyze data in real time.​</p><p><img src="/assets/img/fr/maxi-phyling.png" alt="Maxi-Phyling acquisition unit"></p><h3 id="technical-specifications" tabindex="-1"><a class="header-anchor" href="#technical-specifications"><span>Technical specifications</span></a></h3><table><thead><tr><th>Specification</th><th>Value</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Dimensions</td><td>77x49.5x19.30 mm</td></tr><tr><td>Weight</td><td>100g</td></tr><tr><td>Battery life</td><td>9h</td></tr><tr><td>Connectivity</td><td>Wifi, Bluetooth (BLE)</td></tr><tr><td>Sampling frequency</td><td>Up to 1kHz</td></tr><tr><td>Embedded sensors</td><td>3-axis accelerometer, 3-axis gyroscope, 3-axis magnetometer, multi-band GPS (10Hz)</td></tr><tr><td>Water resistance</td><td>IPX7</td></tr></tbody></table><h2 id="quick-start" tabindex="-1"><a class="header-anchor" href="#quick-start"><span>Quick start</span></a></h2><p>Press the ON button for 0.5 seconds to turn it on; the LED turns green. To start a recording, press the REC button; the LED then turns blue.</p><p>Once turned on, the Maxi-Phyling can be fully controlled with the Phyling application from a Maxi-Hub or from the Phyling cloud application <a href="https://app.phyling.fr" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">https://app.phyling.fr</a>.</p><h2 id="led-color-code" tabindex="-1"><a class="header-anchor" href="#led-color-code"><span>LED color code</span></a></h2><p>An LED provides all the information about the state of the Maxi-Phyling:</p><ul><li>⚪ <strong>White</strong>: the Maxi-Phyling is initializing, shutting down or is in <a href="/en/hardware/maxi-phyling.html#recovery-mode" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Recovery mode</a> (after a record).</li><li>🟢 <strong>Green</strong>: the Maxi-Phyling is ready to start a recording</li><li>🔵 <strong>Blue</strong>: the Maxi-Phyling is recording data</li><li>🟣 <strong>Purple</strong>: the Maxi-Phyling is in <a href="/en/hardware/maxi-phyling.html#hotspot-mode" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Hotspot mode</a></li><li>🟡 <strong>Yellow</strong>: the Maxi-Phyling is in <a href="/en/hardware/maxi-phyling.html#usb-mode-cloud-transfer" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">USB mode</a></li><li>🔴 <strong>Red</strong>: there is a problem, indicated by the number of blinks before shutdown <ul><li><strong>x2</strong>: Configuration error (invalid module, badly formatted file, etc.)</li><li><strong>x3</strong>: GPS not working (if it is not essential, disable it or set <code>&quot;important&quot;: false</code> in its configuration)</li><li><strong>x4</strong>: SD card full: you can empty it manually in USB mode or in Hotspot mode</li><li><strong>x5</strong>: Settings file error (Device, Wifi, Calibration files, etc.) or failure of an automatic sensor calibration (green blink if it succeeded)</li><li><strong>x6</strong>: An error occurred during an update (green blink if it worked)</li><li><strong>No blinking</strong>: Other problem</li></ul></li><li><strong>Green blinking</strong> with 0.5s off every 3s: one of the sensors defined as &quot;important&quot; is not connected (see in the <a href="/en/software/realtime.html#maxi-phyling-configuration" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">settings</a> how to define a sensor as important)</li><li><strong>Red blinking</strong> for 0.5s every 5s: less than 15% battery remaining</li><li><strong>Red at startup</strong> before initialization: there is an initialization error; turn the Maxi-Phyling off and on again</li></ul><h2 id="power-on-recording-and-usage-modes" tabindex="-1"><a class="header-anchor" href="#power-on-recording-and-usage-modes"><span>Power on, recording and usage modes</span></a></h2><p>The Maxi-Phyling has 2 buttons: an <strong>ON/OFF</strong> button and a <strong>REC</strong> button.</p><ul><li>To turn the Maxi-Phyling on or off, hold the ON/OFF button for 0.5s</li><li>To start or stop a recording, press the REC button</li><li>A 3s long press on both ON/OFF and REC buttons while the Maxi-Phyling is off switches to <a href="/en/hardware/maxi-phyling.html#hotspot-mode" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Hotspot mode</a></li><li>A 3s long press on the ON/OFF button while the Maxi-Phyling is off switches to <a href="/en/hardware/maxi-phyling.html#usb-mode-cloud-transfer" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">USB mode</a></li></ul><h3 id="recovery-mode" tabindex="-1"><a class="header-anchor" href="#recovery-mode"><span>Recovery mode</span></a></h3><p>Recovery mode allows you to retrieve the data of a Mini-Phyling that failed to send all its data to the Maxi-Phyling.</p><p>Conditions to activate recovery mode:</p><ul><li>The Maxi-Phyling and the Mini-Phyling are at least on version v6.6.6.</li><li>The Mini-Phyling have &quot;Recovery&quot; mode enabled in their configuration (<code>&quot;useRecovery&quot;: true</code> after <code>use_ble</code>).</li></ul><p>How it works: at the end of a recording, the Maxi-Phyling switches to recovery mode (WHITE LED), and all Mini-Phyling with recovery mode enabled send their data to the Maxi-Phyling. Once the data is received, the Maxi-Phyling exits recovery mode and returns to normal mode (GREEN LED).</p><p>During recovery mode, if you press the REC button, the Maxi-Phyling returns to normal mode (GREEN LED) and the Mini-Phyling stop sending their data.</p><h2 id="charging" tabindex="-1"><a class="header-anchor" href="#charging"><span>Charging</span></a></h2><p>The Maxi-Phyling charges only with the magnetic power cable supplied by Phyling. A white LED lit next to the charger indicates that the Maxi-Phyling is charging; it turns off when the Maxi-Phyling is fully charged.</p><h2 id="inertial-measurement-unit-imu" tabindex="-1"><a class="header-anchor" href="#inertial-measurement-unit-imu"><span>Inertial measurement unit (IMU)</span></a></h2><p>The IMU returns 6 values (accelerations and angular velocities for the 3 directions). The axes of the unit are defined in the following diagram. For all applications where positioning matters (notably rowing and kayaking), make sure to place the unit with the X axis pointing in the direction of travel.</p><p><img src="/assets/img/all/maxi-phyling-axes.png" alt="Orientation of the Maxi-Phyling IMU axes"></p><h2 id="data-retrieval" tabindex="-1"><a class="header-anchor" href="#data-retrieval"><span>Data retrieval</span></a></h2><p>On a Maxi-Hub, data is automatically downloaded to the Phyling Hub when the Maxi-Phyling connects to it and a recording is finished. It appears in the &quot;New data&quot; table (see the <a href="/en/software/data.html" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Data</a> tab). This data must then be associated with one or more athletes, optionally adding other information such as an exercise and a comment.</p><p>On the Phyling cloud application <a href="https://app.phyling.fr" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">https://app.phyling.fr</a>, the Maxi-Phyling automatically uploads its data as soon as the recording ends if it is connected to a WiFi network preconfigured <a href="/en/software/realtime.html#wifi-settings" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">here</a>. It appears in the &quot;New data&quot; table (see the <a href="/en/software/data.html" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Data</a> tab). This data must then be associated with one or more athletes, optionally adding other information such as an exercise and a comment.</p><h3 id="usb-mode-cloud-transfer" tabindex="-1"><a class="header-anchor" href="#usb-mode-cloud-transfer"><span>USB mode &amp; Cloud transfer</span></a></h3><p>With the Maxi-Phyling off, press and hold the ON/OFF button until the LED turns yellow. The Maxi-Phyling is then in USB mode. Simply connect the Maxi-Phyling power cable to a USB-A port and the computer will detect the Maxi-Phyling as a USB drive. You can access all the recordings stored on it. Go to the <code>data/</code> folder to find a recording named after its start time.</p><p>To exit USB mode, restart the Maxi-Phyling.</p><p>To import an activity into the Phyling Cloud application, simply go to the application from a web browser at <a href="https://app.phyling.fr/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">app.phyling.fr</a> and log in with your username and password. In the application, go to the &quot;Data&quot; tab, click the &quot;Import&quot; button above the data table and select the recording&#39;s txt file to import.</p><h2 id="configuration" tabindex="-1"><a class="header-anchor" href="#configuration"><span>Configuration</span></a></h2><p>The Maxi-Phyling can be configured through several configuration files stored in its memory and accessible from Hotspot mode or via the application. We recommend configuring from the application, which is detailed <a href="/en/software/realtime.html#maxi-phyling-configuration" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">here</a>.</p><h3 id="calibration" tabindex="-1"><a class="header-anchor" href="#calibration"><span>Calibration</span></a></h3><p>The sensor calibration of a Maxi-Phyling is also defined in a configuration file. Find more information about the calibration file, the calibration procedure in the application and the different types of calibration <a href="/en/software/realtime.html#calibration" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">here</a>.</p><h3 id="hotspot-mode" tabindex="-1"><a class="header-anchor" href="#hotspot-mode"><span>Hotspot mode</span></a></h3><p>To configure a Maxi-Phyling, and in particular the Hub it must connect to, there is a Hotspot mode. With the Maxi-Phyling off, press the 2 buttons ON/OFF and REC at the same time for 3s. The LED turns purple. The Maxi-Phyling then broadcasts a Wifi network bearing its name and number (for example: <code>Maxi_Phyling_42</code>). Connect with the password &quot;hellophyling&quot;, then enter the address <a href="http://192.168.1.42" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">http://192.168.1.42</a> in a browser to access the configuration interface.</p><p><img src="/assets/img/fr/mode-hotspot-new-1bis.png" alt="Hotspot mode interface with the Wifi networks tab"><img src="/assets/img/fr/maxi_settings_hot_spot_v3.png" alt="Hotspot mode interface with the Wifi networks tab"></p><h4 id="wifi-network-configuration" tabindex="-1"><a class="header-anchor" href="#wifi-network-configuration"><span>Wifi network configuration</span></a></h4><p>For a connection through a Maxi-Hub, the Maxi-Phyling must connect to the Maxi-Hub&#39;s Wi-Fi network to transmit their data and make it visible in the application. The networks they are allowed to connect to are listed in the Wi-Fi Networks section of Hotspot mode. To add a network, add a new entry to the list or edit an existing network. Don&#39;t forget to update before leaving the interface.</p><p>For a connection to the Cloud application, you need a Maxi-Phyling V3 running version V7.0.0 or higher. Put the Maxi-Phyling in Hotspot mode and enter one or more Wi-Fi networks, then select app.phyling.fr as the connection server. Save the changes and restart the Maxi-Phyling. It will automatically connect to the first known Wi-Fi network it finds.</p><p><em>Note: Maxi-Phyling units can connect to a phone&#39;s connection sharing (hotspot). Make sure to check the &quot;Maximize Compatibility&quot; option on iOS or enable the &quot;2.4 GHz&quot; option on Android.</em></p><h4 id="change-the-maxi-phyling-configuration" tabindex="-1"><a class="header-anchor" href="#change-the-maxi-phyling-configuration"><span>Change the Maxi-Phyling configuration</span></a></h4><p>Each Maxi-Phyling has its own configuration with a list of modules (IMU, GPS, heart rate, etc.). In Hotspot mode, you can change the configuration in the &quot;Config&quot; menu.</p><div class="hint-container warning"><p class="hint-container-title">Warning</p><p>This configuration mode using the raw file is risky: some configurations may not be understood by the Maxi-Phyling and prevent it from restarting properly.<br> Before changing the configuration, contact the Phyling team to avoid applying an incorrect configuration.</p></div><h4 id="add-a-heart-rate-sensor-or-a-mini-phyling-to-the-configuration" tabindex="-1"><a class="header-anchor" href="#add-a-heart-rate-sensor-or-a-mini-phyling-to-the-configuration"><span>Add a heart rate sensor or a Mini-Phyling to the configuration</span></a></h4><p>To add heart rate sensors or a Mini-Phyling, this can be done from the hotspot / Config menu. You can run a Bluetooth sensor scan and then simply copy/paste the configuration of the module to add.</p><div class="hint-container warning"><p class="hint-container-title">Warning</p><p>For some heart rate sensors, the Maxi-Phyling may not detect their name. In that case, the sensor will be called &quot;NO NAME&quot;, and you will only see its MAC address.</p></div><div class="hint-container warning"><p class="hint-container-title">Warning</p><p>Make sure to respect the <a href="https://stph.scenari-community.org/bdd/0/co/json02.html" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">JSON</a> format in the configuration.</p></div><p><img src="/assets/img/all/mode-hotspot-config.png" alt="Hotspot mode interface with the Config tab"></p><h4 id="empty-a-maxi-phyling-s-memory" tabindex="-1"><a class="header-anchor" href="#empty-a-maxi-phyling-s-memory"><span>Empty a Maxi-Phyling&#39;s memory</span></a></h4><p>Even once the data has been downloaded to the application, it remains stored in the Maxi-Phyling. To avoid saturating the memory, it is best to delete all the data from time to time. To do so, click the &quot;Delete all records&quot; button; the LED turns white. Then wait until it turns purple again. This operation can take a very long time if there is a lot of data.</p><div class="hint-container warning"><p class="hint-container-title">Warning</p><p>For your Maxi-Phyling to work properly, do not modify the other tabs of Hotspot mode.</p></div><h4 id="update-via-hotspot-mode" tabindex="-1"><a class="header-anchor" href="#update-via-hotspot-mode"><span>Update via Hotspot mode</span></a></h4><p>Updating a Maxi-Phyling brings fixes and new features. Update files are made available to Managers as soon as they are released on the Cloud application.</p><div class="hint-container tip"><p class="hint-container-title">Note</p><p>Updating a Maxi-Phyling can also be done directly from the application in the Real time tab (see <a href="/en/software/realtime.html#maxi-phyling-configuration" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Maxi-Phyling configuration</a>).</p></div><h5 id="on-the-phyling-cloud-application" tabindex="-1"><a class="header-anchor" href="#on-the-phyling-cloud-application"><span>On the Phyling Cloud application</span></a></h5><p>The update is available in the Settings tab, under the <strong>&quot;Releases&quot;</strong> menu. To get the latest version, download the one with the highest numbers (for example, version <code>v6.6.4</code> is more recent than version <code>v6.6.3</code>). A .bin file is available in your download folder.</p><p><img src="/assets/img/all/app_releases_maxi.png" alt="Maxi-Phyling update files"></p><h5 id="on-the-maxi-phyling-hotspot-mode" tabindex="-1"><a class="header-anchor" href="#on-the-maxi-phyling-hotspot-mode"><span>On the Maxi-Phyling Hotspot mode</span></a></h5><p><img src="/assets/img/all/hotspot_maxi_update.png" alt="Hotspot mode interface with the Config tab"></p><ol><li>Click <strong>&quot;Update code&quot;</strong>.</li><li>Import the .bin update file.</li><li>The Maxi-Phyling updates and restarts automatically.</li></ol>',64)])])}]]),r=JSON.parse('{"path":"/en/hardware/maxi-phyling.html","title":"Maxi-Phyling","lang":"en-US","frontmatter":{"description":"Maxi-Phyling Overview This is the heart of Phyling technology: a unique, versatile unit that records all your data at high frequency. Compact, it fits anywhere. Its processing p...","head":[["script",{"type":"application/ld+json"},"{\\"@context\\":\\"https://schema.org\\",\\"@type\\":\\"Article\\",\\"headline\\":\\"Maxi-Phyling\\",\\"image\\":[\\"https://docs.phyling.fr/staging/assets/img/fr/maxi-phyling.png\\",\\"https://docs.phyling.fr/staging/assets/img/all/maxi-phyling-axes.png\\",\\"https://docs.phyling.fr/staging/assets/img/fr/mode-hotspot-new-1bis.png\\",\\"https://docs.phyling.fr/staging/assets/img/fr/maxi_settings_hot_spot_v3.png\\",\\"https://docs.phyling.fr/staging/assets/img/all/mode-hotspot-config.png\\",\\"https://docs.phyling.fr/staging/assets/img/all/app_releases_maxi.png\\",\\"https://docs.phyling.fr/staging/assets/img/all/hotspot_maxi_update.png\\"],\\"dateModified\\":\\"2026-10-01T14:49:06.000Z\\",\\"author\\":[]}"],["meta",{"property":"og:url","content":"https://docs.phyling.fr/staging/en/hardware/maxi-phyling.html"}],["meta",{"property":"og:site_name","content":"Phyling docs"}],["meta",{"property":"og:title","content":"Maxi-Phyling"}],["meta",{"property":"og:description","content":"Maxi-Phyling Overview This is the heart of Phyling technology: a unique, versatile unit that records all your data at high frequency. Compact, it fits anywhere. Its processing p..."}],["meta",{"property":"og:type","content":"article"}],["meta",{"property":"og:image","content":"https://docs.phyling.fr/staging/assets/img/fr/maxi-phyling.png"}],["meta",{"property":"og:locale","content":"en-US"}],["meta",{"property":"og:locale:alternate","content":"fr-FR"}],["meta",{"property":"og:updated_time","content":"2026-10-01T14:49:06.000Z"}],["meta",{"property":"article:modified_time","content":"2026-10-01T14:49:06.000Z"}],["link",{"rel":"alternate","hreflang":"fr-fr","href":"https://docs.phyling.fr/staging/hardware/maxi-phyling.html"}]]},"git":{"createdTime":1790866146000,"updatedTime":1790866146000,"contributors":[{"name":"Claude","username":"Claude","email":"noreply@anthropic.com","commits":1,"url":"https://github.com/Claude"},{"name":"Claude Sonnet 5.5","username":"","email":"noreply@anthropic.com","commits":1}]},"readingTime":{"minutes":5.83,"words":1749},"filePathRelative":"en/hardware/maxi-phyling.md","autoDesc":true}')}}]);